llenges, prioritizing them based on urgency and impact 2. Break down larger problems into manageable components to reduce overwhelm 3. Seek feedback from trusted peers or mentors to gain new insights and solutions 4. Assign specific action items for each identified issue to ensure accountability 5. Use tools like a SWOT analysis to better understand the context of challenges 6. Regularly review progress on resolving issues and adjust strategies as needed 7. Communicate openly with stakeholders about your efforts and seek their support 8. Reflect on past mistakes to identify patterns and avoid repeating them 9. Engage in training or skill development to address personal gaps contributing to the challenges 10. Celebrate small wins to maintain motivation and build momentum toward larger resolutions 11. By effectively acknowledging problems and taking proactive steps to resolve them, you can turn this stage into a foundation for meaningful growth, collaboration, and long-term success"], "actionable_steps": [{"description": "Create a list of challenges, prioritizing them based on urgency and impact"}, {"description": "Break down larger problems into manageable components to reduce overwhelm"}, {"description": "Seek feedback from trusted peers or mentors to gain new insights and solutions"}, {"description": "Assign specific action items for each identified issue to ensure accountability"}, {"description": "Use tools like a SWOT analysis to better understand the context of challenges"}, {"description": "Regularly review progress on resolving issues and adjust strategies as needed"}, {"description": "Communicate openly with stakeholders about your efforts and seek their support"}, {"description": "Reflect on past mistakes to identify patterns and avoid repeating them"}, {"description": "Engage in training or skill development to address personal gaps contributing to the challenges"}, {"description": "Celebrate small wins to maintain motivation and build momentum toward larger resolutions"}, {"description": "By effectively acknowledging problems and taking proactive steps to resolve them, you can turn this stage into a foundation for meaningful growth, collaboration, and long-term success"}]}, {"id": "value_contribution", "title": "Value Contribution to Higher Dimensions", "paragraphs": ["The employee's growth and development will have a positive impact on the team and organization, contributing to a more positive and productive work environment.", "As the employee becomes more self-aware and takes responsibility for their actions, they will be better equipped to work collaboratively with others and contribute to team goals.", "By investing in the employee's growth and development, we can create a more effective and efficient organization that is better equipped to achieve its goals."]}], "report_type": "employee"}]}	2026-05-06 14:35:57.226936+00	2026-05-06 14:35:57.226936+00
37	HR-EMP-00055	SUB-ASSESSMENT-HR-EMP-00055-2D-3304-Self-3305	Assessment Cycle - 3291	{"header": {"cycle_name": "Assessment Cycle - 3291", "designation": "Employee", "employee_id": "HR-EMP-00055", "report_type": "1D - Individual Assessment Growth Report", "stage_scores": [{"score": "1.02", "stage": "Honeymoon", "percentage": "20.4", "final_value": "1.02", "final_percentage": "20.4"}, {"score": "1.34", "stage": "Self-Introspection", "percentage": "26.9", "final_value": "1.34", "final_percentage": "26.9"}, {"score": "1.36", "stage": "Soul-Searching", "percentage": "27.2", "final_value": "1.36", "final_percentage": "27.2"}, {"score": "1.27", "stage": "Steady State", "percentage": "25.4", "final_value": "1.27", "final_percentage": "25.4"}], "employee_name": "HR-EMP-00055", "submission_id": "SUB-ASSESSMENT-HR-EMP-00055-2D-3304-Self-3305", "dominant_stage": "Soul-Searching", "generated_date": "06 May 2026", "dimension_label": "1D - Individual Assessment", "dominant_sub_stage": "Deep Frustration - Soul-Searching", "questionnaire_text": "Self"}, "status": "ok", "reports": [{"title": "Individual Self-Assessment Report", "sections": [{"id": "purpose", "title": "Purpose of the Assessment", "paragraphs": ["This assessment was conducted to gain a deeper understanding of the employee's current behavioral stage, emotional state, and psychological tendencies. The goal is to provide a personalized report that highlights strengths, areas for development, and growth opportunities.", "The assessment focused on the 1D dimension, which covers the employee's individual behavioral patterns and emotional state. This report aims to provide insights that can help the employee navigate their personal and professional growth.", "By understanding the employee's current stage and tendencies, we can identify areas for improvement and develop strategies for sustainable growth and self-awareness."]}, {"id": "overview", "title": "Dimension Overview & Scope", "paragraphs": ["The 1D dimension assesses an individual's behavioral patterns, emotional state, and psychological tendencies. It provides insights into their strengths, weaknesses, and growth opportunities.", "The scope of this assessment includes analyzing the employee's behavioral stage, emotional state, and psychological profile. It does not cover mental health or label individuals.", "The report will provide an overview of the employee's current stage, behavioral indicators, and tendencies, as well as recommendations for personal growth and development."]}, {"id": "inputs", "title": "Inputs & Assessment Instruments", "paragraphs": ["The assessment was based on the employee's self-reported questionnaire data.", "The ChaturVima behavioral stages framework was used to analyze the employee's behavioral patterns and emotional state.", "The assessment approach involved analyzing the employee's stage scores, sub-stage scores, and behavioral indicators to gain a comprehensive understanding of their current state."]}, {"id": "profile", "title": "Employee Profile Summary", "paragraphs": ["The employee, HR-EMP-00055, is currently assessed in the 1D dimension. The assessment was conducted on May 6, 2026.", "The employee's profile indicates that they are in the Soul-Searching stage, with a dominant sub-stage of Deep Frustration.", "This profile summary provides an overview of the employee's current state, which will be used to inform the rest of the report."]}, {"id": "stage", "title": "Emotional Stage Interpretation", "paragraphs": ["The employee's dominant stage is Soul-Searching, with a score of 3.5 and a percentage of 27.25%. The dominant sub-stage is Deep Frustration, with a score of 3.67 and a percentage of 15.17%.", "The Soul-Searching stage is characterized by individuals putting in significant effort but still struggling to achieve results. They are open to change and willing to adapt but require proper guidance to channel their efforts effectively.", "In the Deep Frustration sub-stage, intense emotional difficulty accompanies a fundamental questioning of fit, values, and purpose. The employee is likely experiencing strong emotions and doubts about their current situation."]}, {"id": "stage", "title": "Emotional Stage Interpretation", "paragraphs": ["The behavioral indicators for the Soul-Searching stage include a willingness to acknowledge mistakes, learn from them, and work diligently to achieve success when supported in the right direction.", "The employee's stage scores indicate that they are also exhibiting characteristics from other stages, including Honeymoon, Self-Introspection, and Steady State. However, the Soul-Searching stage is the dominant stage.", "The stage level score summary table provides a detailed breakdown of the employee's scores across different stages and sub-stages."]}, {"id": "stage", "title": "Emotional Stage Interpretation", "paragraphs": ["Here is the stage level score summary table: \\n| Stage | Score | Percentage |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Honeymoon | 2.62 | 20.43% |\\n| Self-Introspection | 3.45 | 26.89% |\\n| Soul-Searching | 3.5 | 27.25% |\\n| Steady State | 3.27 | 25.43% |", "The table shows that the employee scored highest in the Soul-Searching stage, followed closely by Self-Introspection and Steady State.", "The scores indicate that the employee is currently in a state of transition and growth, with a strong desire to adapt and improve."]}, {"id": "psych_profile", "title": "Psychological Profile & Tendencies", "paragraphs": ["The employee's psychological profile suggests that they are experiencing a mix of emotions, including frustration, doubt, and a desire for change.", "Their tendencies indicate that they are open to feedback, willing to learn from mistakes, and eager to grow and develop.", "However, they may also be prone to feelings of overwhelm and uncertainty, which can impact their performance and well-being."]}, {"id": "drivers", "title": "Internal Drivers & Stressors", "paragraphs": ["The employee's internal drivers include a desire for growth, a need for recognition, and a drive for self-improvement.", "However, they may also be experiencing stressors related to feelings of frustration, uncertainty, and self-doubt.", "These stressors can impact their motivation and performance if not addressed."]}, {"id": "swot", "title": "Individual SWOT Analysis", "source": "frappe_swot", "sub_stage": "Deep Frustration - Soul-Searching", "paragraphs": ["1. Awareness of repeated failures highlights persistence in seeking solutions 2. Acknowledgment of persistent challenges demonstrates a willingness to face reality 3. Motivation to break out of the cycle can drive innovative thinking 4. Deep analysis of failures provides valuable learning for future efforts", "1. Emotional exhaustion can hinder clear thinking and effective problem-solving 2. Tendency to focus on past failures, leading to negativity and self-doubt 3. Difficulty in maintaining morale and engagement during prolonged challenges 4. Risk of blaming others or external factors for challenges instead of taking accountability", "1. Opportunity to identify systemic issues that may have gone unnoticed. 2. Chance to seek external perspectives or mentorship for breakthrough solutions. 3. Possibility to rebuild confidence through small, incremental successes. 4. Opportunity to reset priorities and focus on high-impact areas.", "1. Risk of burnout or disengagement if frustrations persist without resolution 2. Escalation of problems due to inaction or continued ineffective strategies 3. Strained relationships with peers or stakeholders due to unaddressed issues 4. Organizational trust may erode if frustrations are left unresolved"], "swot_lists": {"threat": ["Risk of burnout or disengagement if frustrations persist without resolution", "Escalation of problems due to inaction or continued ineffective strategies", "Strained relationships with peers or stakeholders due to unaddressed issues", "Organizational trust may erode if frustrations are left unresolved"], "strengths": ["Awareness of repeated failures highlights persistence in seeking solutions", "Acknowledgment of persistent challenges demonstrates a willingness to face reality", "Motivation to break out of the cycle can drive innovative thinking", "Deep analysis of failures provides valuable learning for future efforts"], "weaknesses": ["Emotional exhaustion can hinder clear thinking and effective problem-solving", "Tendency to focus on past failures, leading to negativity and self-doubt", "Difficulty in maintaining morale and engagement during prolonged challenges", "Risk of blaming others or external factors for challenges instead of taking accountability"], "opportunities": ["Opportunity to identify systemic issues that may have gone unnoticed.", "Chance to seek external perspectives or mentorship for breakthrough solutions.", "Possibility to rebuild confidence through small, incremental successes.", "Opportunity to reset priorities and focus on high-impact areas."]}, "recommendations": [{"recommendations_title": "Leverage Your Strengths", "recommendations_description": "The fact that you recognize persistent challenges reflects your resilience and determination to improve. This self-awareness is a critical strength that can help you confront and address the root causes of frustrations. Use this stage as an opportunity to analyze what has and hasn’t worked, drawing lessons that can inform your future strategies. Acknowledge the progress you’ve made, even if it seems small, as a way to maintain motivation and perspective."}, {"recommendations_title": "Mitigate Weaknesses", "recommendations_description": "Prolonged frustration can lead to emotional exhaustion, negativity, or a tendency to focus on past failures. To mitigate these effects, prioritize self-care and seek support from peers, mentors, or team members. Avoid falling into a cycle of blame or self-doubt, as this can hinder your ability to move forward. Instead, focus on identifying actionable steps that can help you regain a sense of control and progress."}, {"recommendations_title": "Seize Opportunities", "recommendations_description": "This stage offers a chance to reset and refocus. Seek out external perspectives to challenge your assumptions and uncover new solutions. Collaborate with others to share insights and brainstorm ideas. Use the insights gained from your analysis of failures to develop innovative approaches. Rebuilding confidence through small wins can also create momentum for addressing larger challenges."}, {"recommendations_title": "Address Threats", "recommendations_description": "Deep frustration, if left unaddressed, can lead to burnout, disengagement, or strained relationships with stakeholders. To prevent this, take proactive steps to address the root causes of your frustrations. Communicate openly with your team or leaders about the challenges you’re facing and seek their input. Be mindful of the impact your frustration may have on others, and strive to maintain a constructive and solutions-oriented mindset."}, {"recommendations_title": "Adopt a Balanced Approach", "recommendations_description": "Balance self-reflection with action. While it’s important to understand the reasons behind your frustrations, don’t let analysis become a barrier to progress. Focus on what you can control and take incremental steps to create positive change. Approach challenges with curiosity and a willingness to experiment, viewing failures as opportunities to learn and grow."}], "actionable_steps": [{"description": "Identify the specific sources of your frustration and categorize them (eg, systemic, personal, external)"}, {"description": "Seek feedback from trusted peers or mentors to gain new perspectives"}, {"description": "Break down challenges into manageable components to avoid feeling overwhelmed"}, {"description": "Focus on small, achievable goals to rebuild confidence and create momentum"}, {"description": "Document lessons learned from past 